hncagemixdown_meta.sqlite","source":"original","mtime":"1563267079","size":"26624","format":"Metadata","md5":"d7f135633c147ee00e417e6ddc5673e7","crc32":"bca1a833","sha1":"cf728f68856102c229bbad5104bffacd385de448"},{"name":"usmaradioradia747secondojohncagemixdown_meta.xml","source":"original","mtime":"1750962195","size":"2878","format":"Metadata","md5":"e6edff46b95d9d6054155f2507e52b3b","crc32":"76d5dd52","sha1":"5b12c5feec6674c2cb4127618d5a726a160b51f5"}],"files_count":14,"item_last_updated":1750962195,"item_size":1057913825,"metadata":{"identifier":"usmaradioradia747secondojohncagemixdown","mediatype":"audio","collection":["radiafm","radioprograms","radiostationarchives"],"creator":"Usmaradio","date":"2019-07-22","description":"<h2><strong>Secondo John Cage | workshop & live performance</strong></h2><p>Theory - field recording - manipulation - live electronics - conduction - broadcasting</p><p>\n\n\n\n<br />USMARADIO is a workplace of The School of Radio to develop an innovative radio pedagogy. Workshops, work sessions, meetings, presentations of live performance as sections of the project.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>During the White Night (Notte bianca) of the University of the Republic of San Marino, Alessandro Caccuri and Giulio Urbini - students of Unirsm Design - organized and directed the workshop event \"Secondo John Cage (According to John Cage)”. This project is produced by USMARADIO and The School of Radio: based on the theory, field recording, live electronics and conduction. On the day of event, a group of participants (Unirsm students) recorded and post-produced sounds collected by exploring San Marino. The sounds became materials for this performance broadcasted live on USMARADIO’s stream, and the students have been faced - for the most of them was the first time in life - with microphones, sound machines, modular synths, controllers and radios. Even just taking a look to the images the fun and large involvement are showed: the project was such a special and exciting experience for everyone. Based on the success of event, many other workshop around sound and experimentation in the future are already planned. </p>\n\n\n\n<p>The participants: Lorenzo De Fazio, Valentina Toccaceli, Federico Giulioni, Sirya Cardone, Miriana Cerenzia, Alessia Principi, Daniele Trebbi, Damiano Gennari, Roberto Alesi, Marco Maria Lucidi, Gianluca Torcolacci, Grazia Pestillo, Nicola Colomboni, Elena Porreca.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Technical director: Alessandro Renzi</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Photography: Nicole Marchi & Alberto Guerra</p>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"http://www.usmaradio.org\" rel=\"ugc nofollow\">usmaradio.org</a></p>","licenseurl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-nd/4.0/","scanner":"Internet Archive HTML5 Uploader 1.6.4","subject":"radio art;Radia;Usmaradio","title":"Show 0747: Secondo John Cage (Usmaradio)","publicdate":"2019-07-15 15:34:26","uploader":"radia.fm@gmail.com","addeddate":"2019-07-15 15:34:26","year":"2019","backup_location":"ia906907_18","collection_added":"radiostationarchives"},"server":"ia800700.us.archive.org","uniq":696863771,"workable_servers":["ia800700.us.archive.org","ia600700.us.archive.org"]}